pndtw0 (10x);\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 describe\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 emotional narrowing of attention; describe how emotions impair judgment; suggest strategies.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li57\ri2403\sl343\slmult1\sb169\f2\fs19\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 MODEL\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 ANSWER:\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 Research\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 from\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 Harvard\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 School\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 of\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 Public\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 Health\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 found\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 that\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 angry\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 drivers are 10 times more likely to be involved in a crash. Carlos's anger from the workplace\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li57\ri2461\sl343\slmult1\f2\fs19\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 event did not stay at his desk -- it entered his car with him. Anger causes tunnel vision: attention narrows to the source of the anger, and the road becomes secondary. Judgment becomes\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 impulsive\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 and\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 retaliatory,\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 not\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 measured.\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 When\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 another\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 driver\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 made\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 a\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 normal\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 traffic maneuver that Carlos perceived as disrespectful, his already-activated anger responses ignited. The healthy strategy would have been for Carlos to recognize his emotional state before driving -- sit in the parking lot for 10 minutes, 