i57\ri2929\sl343\slmult1\sb168\f2\fs19\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 MODEL\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 ANSWER:\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 Amy\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 exhibits\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 two\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 dangerous\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 attitude\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 profiles:\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 entitlement\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 --\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 belief that her preferences and pace rightfully take priority over other drivers -- and overconfidence -- the belief that personal skill exempts her from compliance with traffic laws. Both attitudes are well-documented predictors of crash involvement. No level of driving skill can eliminate crash risk from factors outside Amy's control: a child\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li57\ri2967\sl343\slmult1\f2\fs19\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 darting\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 into\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 road,\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 a\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 driver\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 having\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 a\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 medical\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 emergency,\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 an\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 unexpected\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 road\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 hazard. Her habit of cutting off drivers and changing lanes without signaling removes other drivers' ability to anticipate and avoid her. Even if Amy's technique is flawless,\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li57\ri3189\sl343\slmult1\f2\fs19\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 she\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 is\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 causing\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 other\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 drivers\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 to\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 take\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 emergency\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 evasive\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 action\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 around\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 her\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 --\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 and\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 she will eventually encounter someone who cannot. Her belief that laws do not apply to skilled drivers is the definition of overconfidence bias.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li57\sl240\slmult1\sb155\f3\fs18\b0\i1\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100\cf2 PAGE REFERENCE: Module 6 / Section 6.2; Module 4 / Section \expnd-1\expndtw-5 4.2\par
