  \expnd0\expndtw0 exhibits\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 sensation-seeking\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 personality\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 trait\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 --\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 a\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 stable\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 tendency toward seeking varied, intense, and novel stimulation. For sensation-seekers, normal traffic feels understimulating, and the brain's reward system generates impulses toward speed and aggressive maneuvering to meet its stimulation need. However, the specific risks James creates are significant: because kinetic energy increases with the square of speed, James driving at 75 instead of 60 increases his crash energy by more than 50 percent, not just\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li57\ri2783\sl343\slmult1\f2\fs19\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 25. Rapid lane changes without adequate scanning eliminate the safety margin for other drivers. The strategic solution for James is to meet his stimulation need before it demands expression\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 behind\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 wheel:\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 use\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 driving\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 time\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 for\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 an\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 engaging\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 podcast\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 or\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 audiobook\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 so\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 his stimulation need is already satisfied. He can also reframe "controlling the journey" as arriving safely rather than navigating quickly.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li57\sl240\slmult1\sb155\f3\fs18\b0\i1\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100\cf2 PAGE REFERENCE: Module 7 / Sect